at are still `it.todo()`, so it won't need renaming as those land.\n\n**Decision: Keep current name** — it already fits the full intent revealed by the test so far and scales to upcoming modifier tests.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Before:**\n```ts\nexport const policyBasePremiumWithModifiers = (items: QuoteItem[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const base = itemBasePremium(item);\n    const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    total += base + cursedSurcharge;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n```\n- Bindings: `items`, `total`, `item`, `base`, `cursedSurcharge` = 5\n- Invocations: `itemBasePremium()` = 1 → 2\n- Conditionals: ternary `item.cursed ? ... : ...` = 1 → 4\n- Loops: `for` = 1 → 5\n- Assignments: `total = 0` (init), `total +=` = 2 → 12\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n\nTotal: 5 + 2 + 4 + 5 + 12 + 1 = **29**\n\n**After:**\n```ts\nexport const policyBasePremiumWithModifiers = (items: QuoteItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => {\n    const base = itemBasePremium(item);\n    const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    return total + base + cursedSurcharge;\n  }, 0);\n```\n- Bindings: `items`, `total`, `item`, `base`, `cursedSurcharge` = 5\n- Invocations: `itemBasePremium()`, `reduce()` = 2 → 4\n- Conditionals: ternary = 1 → 4\n- Loops: `reduce` (iteration) = 1 → 5\n- Assignments: 0 (no mutation, no `let`) = 0\n- Constants: `0` (initial accumulator) = 1\n\nTotal: 5 + 4 + 4 + 5 + 0 + 1 = **19**\n\n**Mass Change: 29 → 19 (delta -10)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\nConverted the imperative `let total = 0; for (...) total += ...` accumulation into a `reduce`-based expression that directly returns the computed value.\n\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The function now reads as a single expression describing \"sum of each item's premium,\" matching its `const`-style declaration pattern used elsewhere (`basePremiumForItems` still uses a loop with a `Map`, which is appropriate there since it needs grouping state — no forced consistency applied).\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Eliminated the mutable `total` variable and the two-line init/accumulate pattern, removing all assignment mass (6×2 = 12 mass eliminated) at the cost of one added invocation.\n- Considered further duplication removal between `basePremiumForItems` and `policyBasePremiumWithModifiers` (both compute per-item premium and sum), but their per-item logic and aggregation strategy (grouping vs. flat) are conceptually different — forcing a shared abstraction now would reduce clarity for two todo-driven, still-evolving functions. Deferred per Rule 3 guidance to favor clarity over premature DRY.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Converted `policyBasePremiumWithModifiers` from imperative loop with mutable accumulator to a `reduce`-based expression; kept the current name as it already accurately reveals intent.\n**Mass Change**: 29 → 19 (delta -10)\n**Tests**: All 8 passing, 24 todo unaffected"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-20-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added policyBasePremiumWithModifiers(items) which computes per-item base premium (sword=100, amulet=60, staff=80, potion=40, fallback to component rate 25) plus a 50% cursed surcharge on the item's own base premium, then sums across items.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added policyBasePremiumWithModifiers(items) which computes per-item base premium (sword=100, amulet=60, staff=80, potion=40, fallback to component rate 25) plus a 50% cursed surcharge on the item's own base premium, then sums across items.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784918730691},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BSM1sbjLpij5tnhTVTvdJD","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01A4KHXp9mykq8FpQG3KAy3T","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":245,"output":123,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10136,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918730711,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-aa61538c-72d2-45be-b300-8077487b3ea3","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01BSM1sbjLpij5tnhTVTvdJD","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  return { premium: PROCESSING_FEE };\n};\n\nexport const claim = (..._args: unknown[]): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n\nexport const basePremiumForItems = (items: QuoteItem[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of countsByType.values()) {\n    total += premiumForGroup(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number => {\n  return MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n};\n\nexport const policyBasePremiumWithModifiers = (\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const base = itemBasePremium(item);\n    const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    total += base + cursedSurcharge;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918732371},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01A4KHXp9mykq8FpQG3KAy3T","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  quote,\n  claim,\n  basePremiumForItems,\n  policyBasePremiumWithModifiers,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - Quote\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, []);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // Building block of 3 alike components (raw base premium, no fee/modifiers)\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 2 runes -> 50 G\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }]);\n    expect(result).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 3 runes -> 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 4 runes -> 100 G (no block - requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 7 runes -> 175 G\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems(\n      Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }))\n    );\n    expect(result).toBe(175);\n  });\n\n  // \"Alike\" components\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: cursed sword + plain amulet -> 210 G (item-scoped cursed surcharge)\", () => {\n    // policy base premium 160 G (100 sword + 60 amulet); cursed surcharge 50 G\n    // (50% of the cursed sword's base premium, not of the policy total) -> 210 G\n    // before further modifiers and fee.\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(210);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier thresholds\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 and cursed -> both surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 and cursed -> only curse surcharge applies\");\n