PREMIUM`, which more accurately reveals that all item types (regardless of category) are just base-premium lookups\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`itemBasePremium` + supporting constants):\n```\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = { sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40 };\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number => {\n  if (item.type in MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM) {\n    return MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n  }\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n    return BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n  }\n  throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n};\n```\n- Constants: 4 (map literals) + 2 (set literals) + 1 (error string) = 7\n- Bindings: 2 (MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM, COMPONENT_TYPES) + 1 (item param) = 3\n- Invocations: `in` check (2) + property access (2) + `.has()` (2) + `throw`/template (2) = 8\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if`, `if`) = 8 (4 each)\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 7 + 3 + 8 + 8 = **26**\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = { sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40, rune: BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM, moonstone: BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM };\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number => {\n  if (item.type in ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM) {\n    return ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n  }\n  throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n};\n```\n- Constants: 4 (literals) + 1 (error string) = 5\n- Bindings: 1 (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM) + 1 (item param) = 2\n- Invocations: `in` check (2) + property access (2) + `throw`/template (2) = 6\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if`) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass: 5 + 2 + 6 + 4 = **17**\n\n**Mass Change**: 26 -> 17 (delta -9)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Merged `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM` and `COMPONENT_TYPES` into a single `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM` map — the split obscured that all item types are just flat-rate lookups; there was no meaningful behavioral distinction between \"main\" and \"component\" items at this function's level\n- Rule 3 (DRY): Eliminated the duplicated \"check membership, then return a value\" pattern that existed twice (map lookup + set lookup) by collapsing to one map and one conditional\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Removed an entire data structure (`COMPONENT_TYPES` Set) and one `if` branch that added no distinct behavior\n- Mass reduced from 26 to 17, driven by removing the second conditional and second lookup structure\n\nBenefits:\n- Single source of truth for all item base premiums\n- One less branch to reason about/maintain when adding new item types\n- Function now more clearly reveals: \"look up this type's base premium, or fail\"\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Consolidated `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM` + `COMPONENT_TYPES` into a single `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM` map, removing duplicated lookup logic and an unnecessary conditional branch.\n**Mass Change**: 26 -> 17 (delta -9)\n**Tests**: All 15 passing (17 todo unaffected)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-20-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: itemBasePremium now explicitly checks main item types (sword/amulet/staff/potion) and component types (rune/moonstone) via a COMPONENT_TYPES Set, throwing an Error for any unrecognized type instead of silently defaulting to the component rate.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: itemBasePremium now explicitly checks main item types (sword/amulet/staff/potion) and component types (rune/moonstone) via a COMPONENT_TYPES Set, throwing an Error for any unrecognized type instead of silently defaulting to the component rate.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784919370899},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01VtPdLx4BA4u1kH5ZyBDsdW","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-20-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GX1uvxBurPWTyEHwUaFBYU","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-20-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":245,"output":255,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10268,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919370918,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-70ca8b49-65e8-4334-873b-d6de8772ed37","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01VtPdLx4BA4u1kH5ZyBDsdW","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\n\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const base = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers(items);\n  const isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = isLoyalCustomer ? base * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = base * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const premium =\n    base - loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium) };\n};\n\nexport const claim = (..._args: unknown[]): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n\nexport const basePremiumForItems = (items: QuoteItem[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    countsByType.set(item.type, (countsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of countsByType.values()) {\n    total += premiumForGroup(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number => {\n  if (item.type in MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM) {\n    return MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n  }\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n    return BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n  }\n  throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n};\n\nexport const policyBasePremiumWithModifiers = (\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => {\n    const base = itemBasePremium(item);\n    const isCursed = item.cursed ?? false;\n    const hasHighEnchantment =\n      (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n    const cursedSurcharge = isCursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    const highEnchantmentSurcharge = hasHighEnchantment\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n    return total + base + cursedSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n  }, 0);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919373820},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01GX1uvxBurPWTyEHwUaFBYU","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  quote,\n  claim,\n  basePremiumForItems,\n  policyBasePremiumWithModifiers,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - Quote\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, []);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // Building block of 3 alike components (raw base premium, no fee/modifiers)\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 2 runes -> 50 G\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }]);\n    expect(result).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 3 runes -> 60 G (block applies)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 4 runes -> 100 G (no block - requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 7 runes -> 175 G\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems(\n      Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }))\n    );\n    expect(result).toBe(175);\n  });\n\n  // \"Alike\" components\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"basePremiumForItems: 3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = basePremiumForItems([\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(120);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: cursed sword + plain amulet -> 210 G (item-scoped cursed surcharge)\", () => {\n    // policy base premium 160 G (100 sword + 60 amulet); cursed surcharge 50 G\n    // (50% of the cursed sword's base premium, not of the policy total) -> 210 G\n    // before further modifiers and fee.\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(210);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier thresholds\n  it(\"quote: customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount applies\", () => {\n    // amulet base 60 G, no curse/enchantment -> policy base premium 60 G\n    // loyalty discount -20% of 60 = -12 G; first insurance surcharge +10% of 60 = +6 G\n    // (no follow-up discount: this is the customer's first quote)\n    // 60 - 12 + 6 = 54 G + 5 G fee = 59 G\n    const result = quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 2 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(59);\n  });\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\", () => {\n    // 100 G base + 30% high-enchantment surcharge = 130 G\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(130);\n  });\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: sword with exactly enchantment 5 and cursed -> both surcharges apply\", () => {\n    // 100 G base + 50% cursed (50) + 30% high-enchantment (30) = 180 G\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(180);\n  });\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\", () => {\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"policyBasePremiumWithModifiers: sword with enchantment 4 and cursed -> only curse surcharge applies\", () => {\n    // 100 G base + 50% cursed (50) = 150 G, no high-enchantment surcharge\n    const result = policyBasePremiumWithModifiers([\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    expect(result).toBe(150);\n  });\n\n  // Rounding\n  it(\"quote: premium calculation yielding a fractional value -> rounded up (e.g. 98.6 -> 99)\", () => {\n    // staff base 80; high enchantment surcharge +24 (30% of 80) -> item premium with modifiers 104\n    // loyalty discount (2+ years) -20.8 (20% of 104); first insurance +10.4 (10% of 104)\n    // 104 - 20.8 + 10.4 + 5 fee = 98.6 -> rounded up to 99\n    const result = quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 2 }, [\n      { type: \"staff\", enchantment: 5 },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(99);\n  });\n\n  // Edge case: unknown item type\n  it(\"quote: unknown item type -> throws\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"broomstick\" }])\n    ).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (0 years, first contract) -> premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer's second contract with cursed sword (enchantment 7) -> premium 160 G\"\n  );\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - Claim\", () => {\n  // Standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G\");\n\n  // Enchantment threshold vs dragon material\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (50% rule wins, then deductible)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G\"\n  );\n\n  // Deductible per damage event\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages insured sword (500 G) and insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (deductible once per item)\"\n  );\n\n  // Multiple items of the same type\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers two swords, two sword damage entries -> each treated as separate damage with own deductible\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damages array has more entries of a type than policy covers -> claim rejected (throws)\"\n  );\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\n    \"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G) -> cap 2000 G based on unmodified insurance value\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers sword and 3 runes (block) -> insurance sum 1750 G, cap 3500 G (block discount does not affect insurance sum)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"sword insured (cap 2000 G), two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first payout 1400 G remaining cap 600 G, second payout 600 G remaining cap 0 G\"\n  );\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down)\");\n\n  // Edge cases\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references damage entry whose item is not part of the policy -> rejected (throws)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\"claim contains damage entry with amount: -200 -> rejected (throws)\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919373820},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AMaXZkLh7bBjzQxJua2yHG","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-20-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | ta