emoving the item from a working list.\n- **Decision**: Replace `findPolicyItem` + `requireInsuredItem` + the `Set<PolicyItem>` bookkeeping with a single function `takeInsuredItem(availableItems, itemType)` that finds-and-removes (via `splice`) from a mutable local copy of the policy's items. This name directly reveals intent: \"take (and consume) an insured item of this type.\"\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Before:**\n```ts\nconst findPolicyItem = (policy, itemType, excluding) =>\n  policy.items.find((item) => item.type === itemType && !excluding.has(item));\n\nconst requireInsuredItem = (policy, itemType, excluding) => {\n  const item = findPolicyItem(policy, itemType, excluding);\n  if (!item) throw new Error(...);\n  return item;\n};\n\nexport const claim = (policy, incident) => {\n  const claimedItems = new Set<PolicyItem>();\n  const rawPayout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = requireInsuredItem(policy, damage.itemType, claimedItems);\n    claimedItems.add(item);\n    return sum + payoutForDamage(damage, item);\n  }, 0);\n  ...\n};\n```\n- Bindings: `policy, itemType, excluding` (x2 funcs) + `item` (x2) + `claimedItems, rawPayout, damage, sum, item` ≈ 13\n- Invocations: `find`, `has` (x2 uses across both fns), `requireInsuredItem`, `findPolicyItem`, `new Set`, `add`, `reduce`, `payoutForDamage` ≈ 8 → mass 16\n- Conditionals: `!item` check (1), inline `&&` exclusion check inside `.find` (1) = 2 → mass 8\n- Loops: `.find` (1), `.reduce` (1) = 2 → mass 10\n- Assignments: 0 (const only)\n- Constants: error string ≈ 1\n- **Total ≈ 1 + 13 + 16 + 8 + 10 = 48**\n\n**After:**\n```ts\nconst takeInsuredItem = (availableItems, itemType) => {\n  const index = availableItems.findIndex((item) => item.type === itemType);\n  if (index === -1) throw new Error(...);\n  return availableItems.splice(index, 1)[0];\n};\n\nexport const claim = (policy, incident) => {\n  const availableItems = [...policy.items];\n  const rawPayout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = takeInsuredItem(availableItems, damage.itemType);\n    return sum + payoutForDamage(damage, item);\n  }, 0);\n  ...\n};\n```\n- Bindings: `availableItems, itemType, index, item` (1 func) + `availableItems, rawPayout, damage, sum, item` ≈ 9\n- Invocations: `findIndex`, `splice`, `takeInsuredItem`, `reduce`, `payoutForDamage`, spread ≈ 6 → mass 12\n- Conditionals: `index === -1` = 1 → mass 4\n- Loops: `findIndex` (1), `reduce` (1) = 2 → mass 10\n- Constants: error string, `-1`, `1`, `0` for splice/index ≈ 2\n- **Total ≈ 2 + 9 + 12 + 4 + 10 = 37**\n\n**Mass Change: 48 → 37 (delta -11)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Collapsed a two-function chain (`findPolicyItem` → `requireInsuredItem`) plus a manually-managed exclusion `Set` into a single, clearly-named `takeInsuredItem` that expresses the real behavior — take-and-remove one matching item. `claim` now works over a local mutable copy (`[...policy.items]`) instead of threading a side-channel exclusion set.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Removed the duplicated lookup logic that existed across two functions doing almost the same `.find`/exclusion check.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: One function and one array copy replace two functions plus a `Set` plus an extra `.add()` call per iteration.\n- Mass reduced 48 → 37, while readability improved (the \"consume from pool\" concept is now explicit).\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed/merged `findPolicyItem` + `requireInsuredItem` (with `Set<PolicyItem>` exclusion) into a single `takeInsuredItem` using array `splice` on a local copy of policy items — better reveals intent, removes duplication, fewer elements.\n**Mass Change**: 48 → 37 (delta -11)\n**Tests**: All 26 passing, unchanged (6 todo remain as before)"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":21637,"output":1876,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":23